.TH "FLOX\-ENVS" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-envs \- show active and available environments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general options>] envs
     [\-\-active]
     [\-\-json]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
This command can be used to list available environments on the local
machine.
When one or more environments are active, the last activated environment
will be listed first and printed in \f[B]bold\f[R].
.PP
Whenever an environment is used with any \f[CR]flox\f[R] command it is
registered to a user specific global registry.
\f[CR]flox envs\f[R] will list all environments known to it through the
registry.
Environments that are present on the local system may not show up until
they are used the first time.
Similarly, if an environment is changed (e.g.\ deleted and replaced by
an environment with different metadata), the change may not show until
the new environment is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Envs Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-active\f[R]
Show only active environments
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-json\f[R]
Format the output as JSON
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
